            "rawRagKnowledgeFAQ": {
              "query": "The user is asking how to rename a file in Twake Drive.",
              "content": "```json\n{\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"rawFAQKnowledge\": \"If a file's name already exists in the destination, the existing file is quietly replaced. The row ends up updated rather than created. Re-uploading `report.pdf` overwrites the existing one without asking. Work is in progress to replace this with a prompt (\\\"Replace\\\", \\\"Keep both\\\", or \\\"Cancel\\\") plus an automatic-rename option. The rename logic has a known rough edge: because it bumps a trailing number, a photo named `IMG_4521.jpg` would become `IMG_4522.jpg` (likely the next photo's name) instead of something safe like `IMG_4521 (1).jpg`.\",\n      \"whyPotentiallyRelevant\": \"This explains the current behavior of file name conflicts and mentions an upcoming feature for renaming files, which is relevant to the user's question about renaming a file in Twake Drive.\",\n      \"sourceHint\": \"docs_twake_twake_drive_drive_upload.md\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
              "candidates": [
                {
                  "rawFAQKnowledgeId": "raw_faq_knowledge_1",
                  "rawFAQKnowledge": "If a file's name already exists in the destination, the existing file is quietly replaced. The row ends up updated rather than created. Re-uploading `report.pdf` overwrites the existing one without asking. Work is in progress to replace this with a prompt (\"Replace\", \"Keep both\", or \"Cancel\") plus an automatic-rename option. The rename logic has a known rough edge: because it bumps a trailing number, a photo named `IMG_4521.jpg` would become `IMG_4522.jpg` (likely the next photo's name) instead of something safe like `IMG_4521 (1).jpg`.",
                  "whyPotentiallyRelevant": "This explains the current behavior of file name conflicts and mentions an upcoming feature for renaming files, which is relevant to the user's question about renaming a file in Twake Drive.",
                  "sourceHint": "docs_twake_twake_drive_drive_upload.md"
                }
